<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 19 June, from 1269 to 1961.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/france" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1269">1269 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">757 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis IX orders Jews in France to wear a badge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An ordinance of Louis IX required <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> to wear a coloured circle of cloth, the rouelle, on their clothing. It enforced a rule of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-council-of-the-lateran">Fourth Lateran Council</a> of 1215 and marked Jews out for discrimination.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1306">1306 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">720 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Earl of Pembroke defeats Robert the Bruce at Methven</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The army of Aymer de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valence">Valence</a>, Earl of Pembroke, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a>'s Scottish army at Methven during the Wars of Scottish Independence. Bruce, who had seized the throne that year, survived such early defeats and waged a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1718">1718 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">308 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake and landslides devastate Tongwei in Gansu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake of estimated magnitude 7.5 struck Tongwei County in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> Province, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>, and caused tremendous damage. Landslides triggered by the earthquake killed at least 73,000 people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1800">1800 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Moreau defeats the Austrians at the Battle of Höchstädt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Höchstädt on the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, the French under General Jean Victor Marie Moreau defeated the Austrians under Baron Pál Kray. Kray was forced back into Ulm and later withdrew into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, opening the Danube route towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-second-coalition">War of the Second Coalition</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union troops proclaim emancipation in Galveston, Texas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Gordon Granger announced that all enslaved people in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> were free, two and a half years after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emancipation-proclamation">Emancipation Proclamation</a>. The day is celebrated as Juneteenth, a US federal holiday since 2021.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1867">1867 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">159 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Maximilian of Mexico is executed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Maximilian, the Austrian archduke installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> as Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, was shot by firing squad at Querétaro with two of his generals. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-juarez">Benito Juárez</a>'s republic was restored.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1910">1910 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">116 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Father's Day is held in Spokane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonora">Sonora</a> Smart Dodd organised the celebration to honour her father, a widower who raised six children. Father's Day became a permanent US national holiday in 1972.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1953">1953 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius and Ethel Rosenberg are executed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The couple were electrocuted at Sing Sing for passing atomic secrets to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. Ethel's role, in particular, remains disputed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1961">1961 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kuwait gains independence from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An exchange of notes ended the 1899 agreement that made Kuwait a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> claimed the new state, and invaded it in 1990.</p></div></li></ol>
